# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEFAULT DENY.
#
# This working directory holds the whole BS Wealth Finance project: live .env
# files, customer phone numbers, tuned production prompts and ~4.6 GB of
# node_modules. The published repository is PUBLIC and must contain only the
# SDLC documentation and the deterministic tooling.
#
# Everything is ignored, then specific paths are re-included below.
# Do NOT switch this to an allow-by-default list.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*

# --- re-include: repository metadata ---------------------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/AGENTS.md

# --- re-include: THE LATENCY CONSTRAINT -------------------------------------
# latency_budget.yaml is loaded at runtime and validated in CI. It is code,
# not documentation.
!/latency_budget.yaml
!/vaani/
!/vaani/*.py
!/tests/
!/tests/*.py
!/.github/
!/.github/workflows/
!/.github/workflows/*.yml

# --- re-include: SDLC documentation ----------------------------------------
!/docs/
!/docs/voice-platform/
!/docs/voice-platform/**

# --- re-include: deterministic tooling -------------------------------------
!/tools/
!/tools/*.py
# tools/turnsense: the end-of-turn replay, training and verification tooling
# (doc 42). Python only -- its data lives in .tmp/, which stays ignored.
!/tools/turnsense/
!/tools/turnsense/*.py

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hard denials. These win regardless of any re-inclusion above, and exist so a
# future edit to this file cannot accidentally publish them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
*.env
credentials.json
token.json
*.pem
*.key

# Customer data / PII
.tmp/
*.csv
test_contacts.csv

# Tuned production prompts — competitive IP, deliberately withheld from a
# public repository. Remove these only for a PRIVATE repo.
/workflows/

# Tools that EMBED the tuned Telugu prompts or the evaluation scenario sets.
# Excluding /workflows/ alone would not have protected them: patch_gptoss_prompts.py
# carries ~2,457 Telugu characters of live prompt text on its own.
/tools/patch_gptoss_prompts.py
/tools/dump_gptoss_prompts.py
/tools/compare_models.py
/tools/invest_train.py
/tools/loan_train.py
/tools/solar_train.py
/tools/solar_battery.py

# Local state
.claude/
.planning/
.obsidian/
.remember/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
.next/
snapshots/
backups/
task_plan.md
findings.md
progress.md
